cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AnaTele in research or a report, please cite it as below."
title: "AnaTele: evidence-first investigation of ArduPilot flight logs"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Avinash Chandra
    family-names: Gupta
    alias: Avinashistoocool
version: 0.5.0
date-released: 2026-10-30
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Avinashistoocool/AnaTele"
url: "https://avinashistoocool.github.io/AnaTele/"
abstract: >-
  AnaTele is an open-source desktop tool for investigating ArduPilot flight logs (.tlog, .bin, .log).
  It infers flight phases, replays the recorded path in 3D, evaluates a versioned declarative rule pack
  with four explicit result states, and ranks competing failure hypotheses by capped, evidence-family
  support minus contradictions, without assigning probabilities. Every finding links to the exact log
  record. It includes a fault-injection quadcopter simulator and a hash-verified shareable analysis
  format (.ant).
keywords:
  - ArduPilot
  - MAVLink
  - drone
  - UAV
  - flight log analysis
  - crash investigation
  - telemetry
